# Client build-time configuration. Copy to `.env` for local overrides.
#
# Only needed for a SPLIT deployment — client on one host (Vercel, Netlify…),
# Cloudflare Worker on another. For the normal single-origin Cloudflare deploy
# leave this unset: the Worker serves the client, so same-origin is correct.
#
# Set it to the Worker's origin, with no trailing path:
#   VITE_API_ORIGIN=https://boardlink.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev
#
# Two things must line up or the browser will block every request:
#   1. The Worker's ALLOWED_ORIGINS must include the client's origin
#      (see .dev.vars.example) — this drives both the CORS headers and the
#      WebSocket origin check.
#   2. The client's Content-Security-Policy `connect-src` must include this
#      origin. vercel.json already allows *.workers.dev; widen it if the Worker
#      is on a custom domain.
VITE_API_ORIGIN=
